    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0490" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/594½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 20, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: If it meets with your
                    approval I propose to request Viscount Ishii to file with his note of
                    confirmation completing <pb facs="0491" n="445" xml:id="pg445"/> the exchange a
                    confidential memorandum such as the one here enclosed.</p>
                <p>I am hastening this matter as rapidly as possible because it takes him several
                    days to communicate with his Government.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d269-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d269-a1.xml" xpointer="d269-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d269-f1" n="17" xml:id="d269-f1-content">
                <p>In an undated memorandum received by Secretary Lansing on October 22, President
                    Wilson replied: “Dear Mr. Sec’y: This seems to me to meet the case and has my
                    approval. Woodrow Wilson.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
